**Definition 24.1 (actual-width and simultaneous resource model).**
Use Definition 13.2's literal codec for every run above.
An enabled digital Read$(j,p)$ has request length
$7+2\ell(|j|)+2\ell(p)$ and integer-reply length $5+2\ell(|k|)$.
An exact Read has request length $5+2\ell(|j|)$ and rational-reply
length $3+\rho(q)$. A successful raw growth at address $a$ pays
$4|a|+9$ request/reply payload bits. C pays its real inner and
outward growth channels and actual inner Tick separately; AD and
raw block A do not acquire this adapter.

Sum these lengths over the actual selected schedule, with every
End, local acknowledgement, Return/navigation, dispatch, fresh
reference/grant transfer, provider input, copy, clearing and requested
export added. Precision sums in §17 are not binary precision-code
traffic. On the nonnegative unit-history runs a safe reply bound is
$2p+9$ also at $p=0$; for $p\ge1$, $2p+7$ suffices by
Proposition 13.4. Arbitrary rational C entrances and later Adds use
their actual signed integer lengths, without that unit-field bound.

Let $W$ be the largest actual numerator, denominator, integer, counter,
solver or digitizer width over the chosen finite run, including
intermediates. Rational-operation counts multiply by the chosen
exact arithmetic/reduction cost $\mathcal A(W)$; numerical slots
multiply by their actual widths. Add all digitization, frame,
address, allocation and copy work. No source-width bound is silently
a bound on elimination intermediates or arbitrary input numerators.

Simultaneous material includes the actual tree, links and grants;
old/new field Tick buffers; genuine root/dispatch/return/input/output
and provider bindings; finite installed code; earned term, ordinal/
material maps and roster; actual raw and nominal acquisition arrays
when both live; reconstructed old/current fields, present predictions,
$O,D$, inverse/forcing/solve scratch; changing reverse syntax, gap/
block/word records and selector state; parser/pending/request/target/
sealed-reply/adapter stores; producer ingress and pulse records;
every live copy, exported or isolated archive, and cleared retained
arena capacity. Genuine sharing counts once; distinct simultaneous
copies count separately. Clearing pays writes and removes access,
without retrospectively removing constructed capacity.

